{
  "info": {
    "sylid": 1889,
    "subjectCode": "TPG301",
    "syllabusName": "Typography & E-publication (Typography & E-publication)",
    "syllabusEnglish": null,
    "credits": "3",
    "degreeLevel": null,
    "timeAllocation": "30 slots, 1 slot = 90 minutes",
    "prerequisite": "TPG202",
    "description": "This course will explore existing modern typographical ideas and techniques and attempt to expand on students’ typographical range. Students will investigate the communication of content and the emotional qualities of text.\n\nStudents will further develop their visual and conceptual fluency and create integrated communication design solutions. Emphasis will be placed on using typography, aesthetics, and composition to construct meaningful imagery and effectively solve communication problems.\n\nThis course uses the art of typography, aesthetic element,..., to build up ideas and apply them in designing products for graphic design such as: publication, branding systems.",
    "studentTasks": "- Attend more than 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination\n\n- Actively participate in class activities\n\n- Fulfil tasks given by intructor after class\n\n- Use their own laptop in class only for learning purpose\n\n- Read the textbook in advance\n\n- Access the course website (www.cms.fpt.edu.vn) for up-to-date information and material of the course, for online supports from teachers and other students and for practicing and assessment.\n\n- Computer with some version of photograph editing software such as Photoshop, Microsoft Word for written assignments, and POWERPOINT for presentations\n\n- Have color papers, Color Pencils, scissors...\n\n- Complete course's Portfolio with full contents of exercises and submit to the teacher 1 day after the course.",
